  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nAn anomalously strong mid level ridge is centered over the Lower MS \nValley and ILN/s area continues to be in a warm and moist airmass \nwith PWAT values around 2 inches. Surface dewpoints in the lower and \nmiddle 70s combined with high temperatures in the lower 90s across\nthe south will result in maximum heat indices of 95 to around 100 \nacross the south.\n\nThunderstorms have developed along an outflow boundary where \nmoderate instability exists. A gradient of favorable DCAPE exists \nwith the most favorable conditions across southern Ohio. A limiting \nfactor is that the mid level lapse rates and flow becomes less \nfavorable farther south deeper into the ridge axis. Expect gusty \nwinds of 30 to 40 mph from these storms as the outflow pushes \nsoutheast across southern Ohio thru the afternoon. Can not rule out \nan isold strong to severe storm if favorable boundary interaction \nenhances an updraft. Along with the gusty wind threat - storms may \ncontain brief heavy rain.",
